{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "outDir": "dist",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  // WITHOUT THIS, `tsc -p tsconfig.json` TYPECHECKS NOTHING AT ALL.
  //
  // Absent an `include`, TypeScript defaults to `**/*`, which picks up
  // `docs/*.test.ts`. Those violate `rootDir: "src"`, so tsc reports three
  // TS6059 CONFIG errors and stops before checking a single file -- and it
  // exits 0 while doing it. Measured 2026-08-25 by planting a deliberate type
  // error and watching it go unreported.
  //
  // That is the same false-green class ShufflewickPub's own CLAUDE.md documents
  // for `npx tsc --noEmit` (which cannot see inside .vue files and so checks
  // about half that repo while looking green). It matters more here: this
  // package ships TYPESCRIPT SOURCE -- `exports` maps both `types` and `import`
  // straight at `src/**/*.ts` -- so every type error in this repo is inherited
  // by consumers that DO typecheck, via the vendored tarball.
  //
  // See docs/typecheck.md for the 217 pre-existing errors this revealed.
  "include": ["src/**/*"],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "vitest.config.ts",
    "src/ai/mcts-bot.test.ts",
    "src/ai/mcts-cache.test.ts",
    "src/ai/cribbage-bot.test.ts",
    "src/ai-trainer/parallel-simulator.test.ts"
  ]
}
